# Shared DSPy rules (cursor-packs)

When creating or wiring dspy-go modules / interceptors / Create* XML:

- Load `.cursor/skills/dspy-module-patterns/SKILL.md`.

When writing or revising module prompts, signatures, or field descriptions:

- Load `.cursor/skills/dspy-prompt-engineering/SKILL.md`.
- Also load project `.cursor/rules/rules-for-prompts.mdc` if present.

When validation fails, fields look full in logs but parse empty, retries exhaust, or a refinement loop exits early:

- Load `.cursor/skills/dspy-go-debugging/SKILL.md`.
- If the project has `.cursor/skills/dspy-xml-structured-output/SKILL.md`, use it for parser/phase details.

Pipeline job layout (JobRunner, per-job clients) stays in the **project** skill if present (e.g. `pipeline-client-module-pattern`). Do not invent a second job pattern.
